{{!
    @template format_uckk/local/content

    Main course content template for the UCKK course format.

    This is the top-level Mustache template for courses using format_uckk.
    It intentionally delegates the main course rendering to Moodle core's
    course format content template, then replaces only the section rendering
    block with the UCKK section template.

    The UCKK-specific course structure is handled by:
    - format_uckk/local/content/section
    - format_uckk/local/content/section/cmitem
    - PHP output classes in format_uckk\output\courseformat

    This file must remain presentation-only.
    It must not contain business rules, permission checks, archive validation,
    integrity decisions, completion logic, challenge workflows, assembly logic
    or AI policy execution.

    Expected Moodle context:
    {
        "initialsection": {},
        "sections": [],
        "hasnavigation": true,
        "sectionnavigation": {},
        "bulkedittools": {},
        "numsections": 9
    }

    Optional UCKK context may be prepared by output classes, but this template
    should stay compatible with Moodle core_courseformat/local/content.
}}

{{!
    Include the Moodle core course format content template.

    Moodle's course format subsystem uses Mustache inheritance blocks for
    partial overriding. The required override here is the section block.
}}
{{< core_courseformat/local/content }}

    {{!
        Mandatory section override.

        Each course section is rendered through the UCKK section template,
        which is responsible for UCKK visual semantics such as:
        - Orientation
        - Concepts
        - Matière canonique
        - Atelier
        - Preuves
        - Délibération
        - Livrable
        - Évaluation
        - Archive
    }}
    {{$ core_courseformat/local/content/section }}
        {{> format_uckk/local/content/section }}
    {{/ core_courseformat/local/content/section }}

{{/ core_courseformat/local/content }}